 5. 🥊 DSA kills off Resistance Dems 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios. Stock: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Democrats who ooze anti-Trump resistance credibility — even central figures in Trump's impeachments — are struggling to withstand the rise of the Democratic Socialists of America and their allies in party primaries, Axios' Andrew Solender writes. 

 One House Democrat told Axios that "being aggressive on accountability and corruption (such as with impeachment) is not enough." 🔭 Zoom in: Retired U.S. Army Lt. Col. Alexander Vindman , who rose to prominence as a witness in Trump's first impeachment, suffered an upset loss Tuesday in Florida's Democratic primary for U.S. Senate to DSA member Angie Nixon.

 Rep. Dan Goldman (D-N.Y.), the highly visible lead counsel for the House Intelligence Committee during Trump's first impeachment, lost his primary to progressive former New York City comptroller Brad Lander. Rep. Diana DeGette (D-Colo.), an impeachment manager during Trump's second impeachment trial in 2021, lost to a DSA-affiliated challenger. Keep reading . 

 
 
