 6. ☎️ Markwayne Mullin&#x27;s Senate hotline 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin arrives for a House Republican caucus meeting at the Capitol last month. Photo: Tierney L. Cross/Bloomberg via Getty Images Axios' Brittany Gibson, who tracks the Department of Homeland Security, writes: 

 Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin is building a reputation as a Cabinet official willing to do favors for his former colleagues in Congress — even at the risk of backlash from the White House and MAGA.

 Why it matters: Some of Mullin's most high-profile moves — such as pausing ICE agents' traffic stops and delaying border security construction along the Texas border — have come after personal appeals from friends on Capitol Hill. 🔎 Zoom in: Mullin's approach contrasts with that of his predecessor at DHS, Kristi Noem, who was frequently criticized for not communicating with Congress.

 DHS recently moved on concerns from Sen. John Cornyn (R-Texas) about a border plan to build roads and security systems in the Big Bend state and national parks. In May, a call from Sen. Tammy Duckworth (D-Ill.) led to the release from ICE detention of Deisy Rivera Ortega, the immigrant spouse of a U.S. military member. Share this story . 

 
 
